dep, depgraph: one-atom match path, string-keyed atom caches, slot reads, unbounded version caches

Five caches are keyed by (atom, atom.unevaluated_atom): the match caches
of PackageTracker, PackageVirtualDbapi and the composite db, the cross-run
match memo and _highest_pkg_cache. An Atom hashes and compares by its
string through Python-level methods; for plain Atoms the key now holds the
two strings, which finds the same entries without those calls.
PackageVirtualDbapi.match() also skips dep_expand() for a plain
non-virtual Atom (it would return the atom as it is), and
PackageTracker.match() reads the slots of a plain Atom directly.

match_from_list() with one plain Atom and a one-element list is the
resolver's most frequent match. A short path (_match_single) performs the
same tests in the same order for the common atom kinds (no operator, or
> >= < <=, with or without slot) and leaves blockers, wildcards, repo
atoms, = =* ~ and USE dependencies to the original code. The kind of an
atom is computed once and kept in a new slot (_match_kind).

vercmp() and catpkgsplit() get unbounded lru caches (they had 1,024 and
10,240 entries, fewer than the distinct arguments of one run). Both are
pure functions of their arguments.

Fifteen Atom properties that only return one slot (cp, cpv, slot,
operator, use, unevaluated_atom, ...) are replaced on the class by the slot
descriptors themselves, so reading them needs no Python call.

On top of patches 0001-0020, resolve seconds before -> after
(median of the runs, at least 2 per figure):
  start 25.7 -> 24.0, holds 12.9 -> 12.2, masks 27.2 -> 25.4,
  py313 15.8 -> 15.1, bdeps 18.5 -> 17.5, policykit 13.2 -> 12.4
  sum of six 113.3 -> 106.6 (-6.6 s, -1.5 % of the stock sum 447.5)
Patches 0001-0021 together: 447.5 -> 106.6 s (-76 %); 447.5 is the
stock sum of the ladder run of 2026-11-20, stock was not run again here.

Four pieces grouped by theme (matching one atom, and the caches keyed by
atoms); alone on 0001-0009 none of them was distinguishable from noise on
the start state.

Weak spots and what was not checked:
* Relies on Atom.__eq__/__hash__ using the string alone; subclasses keep
  Atom keys.
* A second implementation of part of match_from_list() that has to be kept
  in step with it.
* The two caches now grow without bound for the life of the process (a
  concern for long-running API users, not for emerge).
* The attributes become assignable: a property without a setter raised
  AttributeError on assignment, a slot descriptor does not. Whether any code
  assigns them was not searched.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
